<include>context/python_preamble.prompt</include>

% Goal
Create a tiny deterministic pricing helper used as a fixture for contract-aware test generation.

% Role & Scope
The module exposes one public function, `calculate_refund`, that computes an approved refund amount from an original charge and a requested refund.

% Requirements
- Accept numeric `charge_amount` and `requested_refund` inputs.
- Return the requested refund amount when it is greater than or equal to zero and less than or equal to `charge_amount`.
- Raise `ValueError` when the requested refund violates the contract rules.

<contract_rules>
R1 - In-range refund approved
The function MUST return the requested refund when it is greater than or equal to zero and less than or equal to the original charge amount.

R2 - Over-refund rejected
The function MUST NOT approve a refund greater than the original charge amount.
</contract_rules>

% Deliverables
- Code: `context/contract_rules_test_fixture.py`
